gions. The rollback was approved by a human approver. After rollback, the service reports healthy in all regions with error rate 0.002 on v2.3.0. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy in production and should not be redeployed until the failure is root-caused. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 health check failure."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 84005, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012pYEMfGkG2exhAX6Ld6iNe", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 84005, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012pYEMfGkG2exhAX6Ld6iNe", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 85611, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in production with an error rate of 0.18. v2.3.0 is the most recent production release marked healthy.\n- **Current state:** After the rollback, checkout-api reports healthy in all regions with an error rate of 0.002.\n- **Approval:** The rollback response shows a human approval (\"Approved. Looks right.\").\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback, and the current state. It also notes that v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until someone finds the root cause.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01FLgk1wWPpXUEHYUuNgBF78", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01C7cjrFrWoUVmrnET8Kfdd7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "nam